provider: anthropic (claude-opus-5-5)
request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (The rename changes the shared Todo interface in types. format, storage and commands each read or write that field, so all four units need updating in parallel. To avoid scope creep, output text and ListOptions.includeDone stay the same. storage will still load older JSON files that use `done`.)
round 1: owners types=rejected format=rejected storage=rejected commands=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (Each owner's test change only renames the field, which is exactly what the request asks for, so I approve all four and send the same plan again. The red oracle output comes from acceptance tests that already expect `completed`. They will pass once types renames the field and the other units adopt it.)
round 2: owners types=ok format=ok storage=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc reports no errors and all 16 vitest tests pass. The manifest shows Todo now has `completed: boolean` in place of `done`. All four owners submitted their changes. The only test edits were the approved field renames, and each test still checks the same result as before. storage still reads old files that use `done`. ListOptions.includeDone was kept on purpose, because it's a list option, not a field on Todo.)

